Panfrost: optional read-only vertex-stage SSBOs (PAN_RO_VERTEX_SSBO=1), against Mesa 26.2.4.

Ghostty's GL 4.3 renderer reads a std430 `readonly buffer` from its vertex shader (cell_text.v.glsl), and stock
Panfrost advertises 0 vertex SSBOs ("Too many vertex shader storage blocks (1/0)"). Panfrost keeps vertex side
effects off because IDVS splits a vertex shader into position and varying shaders that may each run (and may
re-shade vertices), and transform feedback runs a second copy of the shader: writes and atomics would repeat.
Reads are idempotent, so they are safe in both IDVS halves; everything else for vertex SSBOs (resource tables
on v9+, sysvals on Bifrost, LD_PKA/LEA_PKA in the compiler) already exists for the fragment/compute stages and
PanVK and is stage-agnostic.

With PAN_RO_VERTEX_SSBO=1 (default off, Bifrost and newer):
- the vertex stage reports 16 shader buffers, like fragment/compute (the GL frontend splits them 8 SSBO +
  8 atomic-counter buffers); vertex images stay at 0;
- panfrost_create_shader_state() removes store_ssbo/ssbo_atomic/ssbo_atomic_swap from vertex shaders (atomics
  return 0) with a one-time warning, before the shader is hashed, so the GPU never sees vertex-stage writes.

